[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: ELK removes measured label collisions without losing semantic edges

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[EVIDENCE]
UID: EV-SDOC-BOARD-ELK-NEIGHBORHOOD-SMOKE
TITLE: ELK removes measured label collisions without losing semantic edges
DEPTH: verified
AUTHORED_BY: llm
SOURCE: Independent Chromium 152 headless DevTools probes at 1440x900 against the live scribe daemon, plus a synthetic pre-layout cap probe; 2026-09-02
STATEMENT: >>>
Against the live generation-14 canon, headless Chromium rendered
WORK-SCRIBE-RPC-AND-SERVICE at two hops as 14 cards and 20 semantic links using
22 ELK-routed path pieces and 15 labels. Bounding-box tests found zero
label-label and zero label-node intersections; stroke sampling across 23 broad
path-box candidates found zero labels intersecting unrelated paths. The prior
custom router on the same neighborhood measured 15 label-label and 10
label-node intersections.

Five Proven_By relations rendered as two labels: one direct edge plus one
labeled trunk shared by a four-source fan-in. That group used six routed pieces.
Selecting MECH-SCRIBE-DEVENV-PROCESS activated the two group pieces associated
with that semantic relation and dimmed the other four without changing the
focal hash. Rapid depth selection from three to one to two settled on the latest
two-hop request with aria-busy cleared. A separate 101-node synthetic star probe
retained its center and clipped to 48 nodes before invoking ELK. The page
reported no runtime, console, log, board-event, or page errors.
<<<
